  "  \\[ A_v = - \\frac { \\mu R_L } { r_p + R_L } = - \\frac { 50 \\times 40000 } { 10000 + 40000 } = - \\frac { 2000000 } { 50000 } = - 40.0 \\]",
  "",
  "* **Step 3: Calculating Miller Input Capacitance \\( C _ { in } \\)**:",
  "  Applying the Miller Effect transformation:",
  "  \\[ C _ { in } = C _ { gk } + C _ { gp } ( 1 + | A_v | ) = 3.0 \\text{ pF} + 2.5 \\text{ pF} \\times ( 1 + 40.0 ) = 3.0 + 2.5 \\times 41.0 = 3.0 + 102.5 = 105.5 \\text{ pF} \\]",
  "  The Miller multiplication increases effective input capacitance by over a factor of 20.",
  "",
  "==== Example 2: High-Bandwidth Electrostatic Cathode-Ray Tube Analysis",
  "",
  "**Problem Statement:**",
